<title>USA: Huntco to acquire Coil-Tec assets.</title>
<headline>Huntco to acquire Coil-Tec assets.</headline>
<dateline>TOWN &amp; COUNTRY, Mo. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huntco Inc, an intermediate steel processor, said Friday it signed a letter of intent to acquire certain assets of Coil-Tec Inc, a wholly owned subsidiary of ARBED Americas Inc.</p>
<p>The primary asset, in addition to inventory, is the Blytheville, Ark. plant of Coil-Tec, which houses a two high temper mill and cut-to-length line designed to produce tempered, panel flat sheets and plates as well as tempered hot rolled steel coils. Huntco does not produce either product.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
